WEBVTT

NOTE
English visual summary of the supplied v4 installation animation; not a speech transcript or structural specification.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Jefferson in Athens: installation at the Ambassador’s residence.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Illustrative finished setting at the main entrance. Sculpture: 100 cm high; exposed base: 120 cm high.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Introduction to the studio’s concrete-base method. Cost and construction time are indicative; final design requires the contractor and licensed structural engineer.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Related base installations in Athens and the proposed location inside the main entrance. Landscaping is illustrative.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Prepare the formwork tube, concrete materials, reinforcement and mixer. Proposed cylinder diameter: 60 cm.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Excavate and assemble the reinforcement grid. Final footing dimensions and reinforcement are determined by the engineer.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Set vertical reinforcement and pour the footing. Vibrate the concrete.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Position and brace the formwork tube; pour and vibrate the cylinder. The top 10 cm fits inside the sculpture.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Proceed only when the engineer confirms that the concrete has cured.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Remove the formwork, grind the spiral seams, finish, prime and paint the base.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Dry-fit the sculpture and confirm its orientation with George Petrides.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Drill and install the threaded bolts as specified by the engineer. Lower and engage the sculpture using the confirmed handling plan.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Install the approved bronze plaque.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:41.292
Complete the surrounding planted setting. Landscaping is illustrative and is to be designed by the residence staff.
